{
  "name": "Schedule: create a Social Poster draft per weekday, optionally scheduled",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "4404ce6d-c45a-5b51-b3ba-8e3cf535aa8d",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -300,
        -40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nThe schedule runs every day at the set time (Europe/Berlin). “Choose today's caption” takes the caption for today's weekday from the seven fields in “Settings”. If today has no caption, the run ends without a post. Otherwise “Create the draft” saves it as a draft in Social Poster.\n\n### Draft or scheduled\nThe default is `mode` = `draft`: the workflow only creates a draft and schedules or publishes nothing. The link to view it is in the output of “Create the draft” under `draft.app_draft_url`. To schedule posts, set `mode` to `schedule`. “Schedule the draft” then schedules it `minutesFromNow` minutes later (at least 5) and confirms it. If your team requires approval, it waits under “Waiting for you”. There is no immediate publishing.\n\n### Setup\nThis template uses the unverified community node `n8n-nodes-social-poster` (tested with version 0.1.1). It runs on self-hosted n8n only, not on n8n Cloud. Install it under Settings → Community Nodes → Install. Guide: https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/\nCreate “Social Poster API” credentials. You get the key in Social Poster under the account menu → AI access → API key for n8n. The base URL is `https://app.social-poster.io` without `/mcp`.\nIn “Settings”, enter your account reference (`acc_…`), an optional link and image URL, and the captions for Monday to Sunday. Set the time on the schedule node, the default is 9:00. Select the credentials on both Social Poster nodes and run it once by hand.\n\n### Customization\nLeave a day empty if nothing should go out. For a longer rotation, read the captions from a spreadsheet.",
        "height": 820,
        "width": 660,
        "color": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "eb8915da-1ff2-522e-9d0c-af6e82c3c3a0",
